[node name="Portal" parent="StartEnd" instance=ExtResource("19_portal")]
editor_description = "The finish at 345 deg. scenes/ring/marble_portal.tscn -- portal.tscn node for node, the same Glow and the same Gate in the finish_gate group, with the marble surround in place of the hell-rock arch and the portal's own effect surface unchanged inside it. Local Z is the pass-through axis along the run, local X the span across the lane."
transform = Transform3D(0.965926, 0, 0.258819, 0, 1, 0, -0.258819, 0, 0.965926, 50.2281, 23, -13.4586)


[node name="Bars" parent="." instance=ExtResource("20_marble_bars")]
editor_description = "Bars across the walkway at 353 deg, in the gap between finish (345) and start (5), and the ONE fixture that survived the clearing of the lane (Ryan, 2026-09-22: \"get rid of all the elements on the ring\") -- because the bake and the harness say it is not decoration. With a finish gate in the scene, standing in it is the win (MatchLapTracker: no checkpoints), so without these bars RingBake links PrisonerStart to PrisonerEnd the SHORT way round, 18.06 m backwards through this gap instead of 288.15 m forwards, and a bot runner walks straight to the portal: 7 of 10 harness matches went unresolved at 101-129 one-shot rounds. With them, 10 of 10 resolve. They stand outside the 340 deg run, behind the finish, so they are in no shot of the lane. assets/models/marble_bars.glb: an iron portcullis in a marble frame in the rotunda's own architecture -- ashlar plinth, fluted pilaster jambs, a 6.00 x 6.20 m mouth under a semicircular head, a cornice moulding -- the iron the same near-black as the cell bars. IT SPANS THE WALKWAY WALL TO LIP (Ryan, 2026-09-23: \"the gate doesnt block anyone from going past it to the portal\"). It did not: on rock_bars' inherited 10.6 m centred on the lane at r 52.0 the collider reached r 46.7007..57.3005, and the walkway runs r 46.7..59.55 -- 2.2495 m of open floor outboard of the gate, measured headless off this scene, and a body walked ROUND it to the portal rather than through it. The gate is now 12.85 m wide and its centre stands at r 53.125, so the collider reaches the inner lip and the cell wall and there is no floor left to walk round; the extra 2.25 m went into the flanking ashlar field, mouth, jambs and bars all unchanged. Everything else is still rock_bars': 8.5 m tall, origin the base centre, and no gap anywhere wider than 0.38 m. Local X (12.85 m) runs radially across the lane, local Z along it. tests/test_marble_gate.gd drives a capsule at it from across the whole walkway and is what says it holds."
transform = Transform3D(0.992546, 0, 0.121869, 0, 1, 0, -0.121869, 0, 0.992546, 52.729014, 23, -6.474309)

[node name="Watch" type="Node3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "Where the AI guard's scan rests when it has nothing remembered: five points spread round the lap, so the crosshair sweeps the lane instead of staring at one bearing. Markers only -- nothing is drawn and nothing collides. They are all the Sections node left behind when the course came off the lane (Ryan, 2026-09-22: \"for the marble level, can you just get rid of all the elements on the ring?\"), kept because they are not an element ON the ring: deleting them would change how the guard plays, which is not what was asked. Named by bearing now that there are no stretches to name them after."

